date-released: 2026-05-22
abstract: >
  ARISE (Automated River Intelligence System for Early-Warning) is an automated hybrid
  flood forecasting and early-warning system operationally deployed in the Tlawng River
  Basin, Mizoram, Northeast India. This repository contains the Medium-Term sub-system:
  XGBoost-based bias correction of ECMWF ensemble forecasts feeds a hybrid
  HEC-HMS – GRU – XGBoost model chain to forecast river stage at 3-, 5-, and 7-day
  lead times, classified into a unified five-tier danger level scheme.
